---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import { registryEntries } from '../../config/registry';

const agentEntries = registryEntries.filter(
  (e) => e.vaultKeywords?.length || e.copyPath
);
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Cursor + Cleo Vault"
  description="Full agent playbook — vault scan to implementation without manual copy paths"
>
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>Cursor + Cleo Vault</h1>
    <p class="page-lead">
      Canonical playbook for <strong>Enzo</strong> and Cursor: scan Obsidian vault → resolve registry
      → open implementation files automatically. Humans do not hunt copy paths by hand.
    </p>
    <p>
      This page mirrors <code>AGENTS.md</code> in the repo. Cursor also loads
      <code>.cursor/rules/cleo-vault-to-ds.mdc</code> and skill
      <code>cleo-second-brain-query</code> when vault work is in scope.
    </p>

    <h2>Automatic workflow</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>
        <strong>Read vault</strong> — Cleo Second Brain (iCloud Obsidian). Start in
        <code>wiki/synthesis/</code>. Never edit <code>raw/</code>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Resolve UI</strong> — Match vault text to registry via
        <code>vaultKeywords</code> in <a href="/registry">Registry</a> or
        <code>src/lib/resolve-registry-from-text.ts</code>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Build plan</strong> — <code>buildImplementationPlan(entryId)</code> returns
        <code>copyPath</code>s, doc hrefs, related entries, and pattern pages.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Execute</strong> — Open every implementation file, doc source under
        <code>src/pages</code>, <code>src/styles/tokens.css</code>, and
        <code>CLEO_DESIGN_SYSTEM_PROMPT.md</code>. Do not ask the engineer to paste paths or click
        Copy on block pages.
      </li>
    </ol>

    <h2>Default Julie MVP stack</h2>
    <p>
      If vault text is about Julie pilot, daily note, or iPad without a narrower match:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Primary: <a href="/blocks/visit-shell">visit-shell</a> —
        <code>src/components/cleo/blocks/VisitShellShowcase.tsx</code>
      </li>
      <li>
        Related: status-strip, stepper, tab-bar, treatment-table, locked-band (see
        <a href="/registry">Registry</a>)
      </li>
      <li>
        Components: <a href="/components/hitl">HITL</a>,
        <a href="/components/ipad-constraints">iPad constraints</a>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Quiet Authority (non-negotiable)</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Tokens from <a href="/foundations/theming">theming</a> / <code>src/styles/tokens.css</code> only</li>
      <li>No Material, default Tailwind, or bright SaaS palettes without Cleo mapping</li>
      <li>Amber accent once per screen</li>
      <li>iPad Safari is acceptance device for Julie MVP blocks</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Copy path on block pages</h2>
    <p>
      The <strong>Copy path</strong> control on component docs is for humans browsing this site.
      <strong>Agents</strong> use the registry table below and <code>registry.ts</code> — never
      instruct Enzo to click Copy.
    </p>

    <h2>Repo files (same truth as this page)</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><code>AGENTS.md</code> — agent entry point</li>
      <li><code>src/config/registry.ts</code> — <code>vaultKeywords</code>, <code>copyPath</code>, <code>relatedIds</code></li>
      <li><code>src/lib/resolve-registry-from-text.ts</code> — keyword → plan</li>
      <li><code>CLEO_DESIGN_SYSTEM_PROMPT.md</code> — full AI system prompt</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Vault keyword map</h2>
    <p>Lowercase phrases in Cleo Vault / Obsidian that resolve to each registry entry.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="vault-map-wrap">
    <table class="vault-map-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Registry id</th>
          <th>Name</th>
          <th>Vault keywords</th>
          <th>Implementation path</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          agentEntries.map((entry) => (
            <tr>
              <td><code>{entry.id}</code></td>
              <td>
                <a href={entry.href}>{entry.name}</a>
              </td>
              <td class="keywords">
                {entry.vaultKeywords?.length ? (
                  entry.vaultKeywords.join(', ')
                ) : (
                  <span class="muted">—</span>
                )}
              </td>
              <td class="path">
                {entry.copyPath ? (
                  <code>{entry.copyPath}</code>
                ) : (
                  <span class="muted">Planned</span>
                )}
              </td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>

<style>
  .vault-map-wrap {
    margin: var(--space-8) 0 var(--space-12);
    overflow-x: auto;
  }

  .vault-map-table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
  }

  .vault-map-table th {
    text-align: left;
    font-size: var(--text-label);
    font-weight: var(--weight-medium);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-label);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-steel);
    padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-4) var(--space-3) 0;
    border-bottom: var(--border-hairline);
  }

  .vault-map-table td {
    padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-4) var(--space-3) 0;
    border-bottom: var(--border-hairline);
    color: var(--color-midnight);
    vertical-align: top;
  }

  .vault-map-table .keywords {
    color: var(--color-steel);
    max-width: 280px;
  }

  .vault-map-table .path code {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    word-break: break-all;
  }

  .muted {
    color: var(--color-steel);
  }
</style>
